; ffbonded_tminff.itp - bonded parameters for the TMINFF mineral sets.
;
; Companion to ffnonbonded_tminff.itp. Each block is guarded by the mineral
; name alone, because these parameters do not depend on the angle force
; constant: the O-M-O stiffness is applied through KANGLE in the mineral .itp
; file, not here. Select with e.g. define = -DMontmorillonite -DMINFF_k500.
;
; Only the terms whose atomtypes the chosen mineral actually defines are
; emitted, so grompp never sees a bondtype referring to an undeclared type.
; Minerals with no hydroxyl groups (quartz, corundum, rutile, periclase and
; the other anhydrous oxides) legitimately contribute nothing.
;
; Bonds: O-H from MINFF; M-O from the MINFF bonded set.
; Angles: M-O-H from Pouvreau, Greathouse, Cygan and Kalinichev,
;         J. Phys. Chem. C 2019, 123, 11628-11638 (k=125.52, theta0=110).
;

#ifdef Akdalaite
[ bondtypes ]
;  i      j     func      b0        kb
Oh      H       1      0.09572   441050
Ob      H       1      0.09572   441050
[ angletypes ]
;  i      j       k     func    th0      cth
H       Oh      Alo     1     110.0   125.52  ; Al(oct)-O-H
#endif

#ifdef Anatase
; no hydroxyl or M-O bonded terms for this mineral
#endif

